2H8a1 1 0 0 1-1-1v-7Z\"></path><path fill=\"currentColor\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M8.776 2.553a.5.5 0 0 1 .671.223l.775 1.55A4.99 4.99 0 0 1 12 4a4.99 4.99 0 0 1 1.778.325l.775-1.549a.5.5 0 1 1 .894.448l-.775 1.55A4.996 4.996 0 0 1 17 9H7c0-1.779.929-3.34 2.328-4.227l-.775-1.55a.5.5 0 0 1 .223-.67ZM10 6.5a.5.5 0 1 1-1 0 .5.5 0 0 1 1 0Zm4.5.5a.5.5 0 1 0 0-1 .5.5 0 0 0 0 1Z\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg><span>Android</span></a></div></div><div class=\"EventDetailsLayout__MobileContent-sc-2554ecc8-5 fAoBgn\"><div class=\"EventDetailsBase__HR-sc-d40475af-3 eSgOkc\"></div><div class=\"EventDetailsFAQ__Container-sc-7130cefd-1 kjqLCB\"><p>DICE protects fans and artists from touts. Tickets will be securely stored in the app.</p></div><div class=\"EventDetailsBase__HR-sc-d40475af-3 eSgOkc\"></div></div></div></div></div><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fschema.org\",\"@type\":\"ScreeningEvent\",\"url\":\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fdice.fm\\u002Fevent\\u002Fbbnr7x-black-narcissus-film-screening-chl0ecurrytomirose-live-15th-jan-live-at-st-giles-london-tickets\",\"name\":\"Black Narcissus: Film Screening & chl0ecurry+tomirose Live\",\"startDate\":\"2026-01-15T19:00:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2026-01-15T23:00:00+00:00\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fschema.org\\u002FOfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"eventStatus\":\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fschema.org\\u002FEventScheduled\",\"location\":{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Live At St Giles\",\"address\":\"Camberwell Church Street, Southwark, London, SE5 8RB, United Kingdom\",\"geo\":{\"@type\":\"GeoCoordinates\",\"latitude\":51.47364,\"longitude\":-0.08961}},\"image\":[\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fdice-media.imgix.net\\u002Fattachments\\u002F2025-12-22\\u002F2fa51aba-158d-48be-8fef-3fdeb30dcee4.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C3508%2C3508\"],\"description\":\"\\\"An extraordinary melodrama of repressed love and Forsterian Englishness - or rather Irishness - coming unglued in the vertiginous landscape of South Asia\\\" - Peter Bradshaw, The Guardian\\n\\n@dashthehengestore x SECRET CEREMONY by @lost.art.media return to St Giles' for a screening of Michael Powell and Emeric Pressburger 1947 classic BLACK NARCISSUS on JANUARY 15th 2026\\n\\nAs always the night will commence with a live musical performance by experimental artists chl0ecurry+tomirose\\n\\nOur previous events have all SOLD OUT so don't delay, grab your tickets while you can!\\n\\nArt by @kieranrid\\n\\nSound as always by @evareadypa and @liveatstgiles\\n\\nFull Peter Bradshaw review https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.theguardian.com\\u002Ftheguardian\\u002F2005\\u002Faug\\u002F05\\u002F3\\n\\n\\\\--\\n\\nA percentage of every ticket sold will be contributed to The Friends of St Giles’\\n\\nThe Friends of St Giles’ was founded in the 1980’s to help raise funds for the repair and maintenance of St Giles.\\n\\nIt recognises that St Giles’ plays a significant role in the secular life of SE5, in particular through the development of community involvement in music and the arts.\",\"offers\":[],\"organizer\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Dash The Henge Store x Secret Ceremony by LOST ART\"}}</script></div><footer class=\"Footer__Wrapper-sc-b4b03d95-1 bXotkg default-footer-background hide-in-purchase-flow\"><div class=\"Footer__MaxWidthWrapper-sc-b4b03d95-2 Footer__PrimaryFooter-sc-b4b03d95-3 ZGZWE btQVbq\"><div class=\"Footer__LogoCol-sc-b4b03d95-6 fGSCng\"><a aria-label=\"DICE\" href=\"/\" class=\"Footer__Logo-sc-b4b03d95-7 ebGIam\"><img width=\"200\" height=\"244\" alt=\"DICE\" src=\"/static/images/dice-fan.gif\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div><div class=\"Footer__Nav-sc-b4b03d95-8 kTXnAq\"><details open=\"\" class=\"FooterNavCol-sc-e5ef781b-0 jLkSXP\"><summary class=\"Description-sc-f5e05090-0 FooterNavCol__NavTitle-sc-e5ef781b-2 irmwOP dsHsU\">Our company<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"FooterNavCol__NavIcon-sc-e5ef781b-1 iFhQbp\"><path st